"Running different sets of tests, for example fast tests vs slow tests, or "
"running them with verbose output"
msgstr ""

#: src/further-ramblings.md:35
msgid ""
"Any complex set of commands that you really should write down somewhere, if "
"only to be able to remember them"
msgstr ""

#: src/further-ramblings.md:38
msgid ""
"Even for small, personal projects it’s nice to be able to remember commands "
"by name instead of ^Reverse searching your shell history, and it’s a huge "
"boon to be able to go into an old project written in a random language with "
"a mysterious build system and know that all the commands you need to do "
"whatever you need to do are in the `justfile`, and that if you type `just` "
"something useful (or at least interesting!) will probably happen."
msgstr ""

#: src/further-ramblings.md:45
msgid ""
"For ideas for recipes, check out [this project’s `justfile`](https://github."
"com/casey/just/blob/master/justfile), or some of the `justfile`s [out in the "
"wild](https://github.com/search?q=path%3A**%2Fjustfile&type=code)."
msgstr ""

#: src/further-ramblings.md:51
msgid ""
"Anyways, I think that’s about it for this incredibly long-winded README."
msgstr ""

#: src/further-ramblings.md:53
msgid ""
"I hope you enjoy using `just` and find great success and satisfaction in all "
"your computational endeavors!"
msgstr ""

